From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 8 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Skip adapter string-tensor export test without onnx

test_adapter_export_rejects_string_tensors (new in 1.28.0) imports the
onnx python package unconditionally, unlike the sibling tests which
guard the import (see test_run_output_does_not_alias_input_passthrough
and test_tree_ensemble_logistic). Add the same skipUnless guard so the
suite passes in environments without onnx installed. Not yet fixed
upstream as of microsoft/onnxruntime main @ 2026-08-08.
---
 onnxruntime/test/python/onnxruntime_test_python.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/onnxruntime/test/python/onnxruntime_test_python.py b/onnxruntime/test/python/onnxruntime_test_python.py
--- a/onnxruntime/test/python/onnxruntime_test_python.py
+++ b/onnxruntime/test/python/onnxruntime_test_python.py
@@ -2195,6 +2195,10 @@ class TestInferenceSession(unittest.TestCase):
             if os.path.exists(file_path):
                 os.remove(file_path)

+    @unittest.skipUnless(
+        importlib.util.find_spec("onnx") is not None,
+        "onnx package is required to build the test model",
+    )
     def test_adapter_export_rejects_string_tensors(self):
         # Regression test: export_adapter previously serialized Tensor::DataRaw()
         # for SizeInBytes() bytes regardless of element type. For string tensors
